### Fendo API — VS Code REST Client Test File
### Install: "REST Client" extension by Huachao Mao
### How to use: Click "Send Request" above any request

@base = http://localhost/fendo/public/api/v1
@token = PASTE_YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 1: AUTH
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### 1. Register new user
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "Password1",
  "password_confirmation": "Password1"
}

###

### 2. Verify OTP (copy otp from register response)
POST {{base}}/auth/verify-otp
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "otp": "PASTE_OTP_HERE",
  "purpose": "register"
}

###

### 3. Login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "Password1",
  "device_name": "VS Code"
}

###

### 4. Get current user
GET {{base}}/auth/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 4b. Refresh token (requires current Bearer token — revokes old, issues new)
POST {{base}}/auth/refresh
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 5. Forgot password
POST {{base}}/auth/forgot-password
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com"
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 2: USER PROFILE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### 6. Get profile
GET {{base}}/user/profile
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 7. Update profile
PUT {{base}}/user/profile
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "currency": "USD",
  "timezone": "America/New_York",
  "venmo_handle": "@johndoe"
}

###

### 8. Get notification settings
GET {{base}}/user/notification-settings
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 9. Update notification settings
PUT {{base}}/user/notification-settings
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "expense_added": true,
  "settlement_received": true,
  "bill_reminder": true,
  "weekly_summary": false
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 3: GROUPS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### 10. Create group
POST {{base}}/groups
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bali Trip 2026",
  "type": "vacation",
  "currency": "USD",
  "simplify_debts": true
}

###

### 11. List groups
GET {{base}}/groups
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 12. Get group (replace 1 with your group id)
GET {{base}}/groups/1
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 13. Generate invite link
POST {{base}}/groups/1/invite-link
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 14. List group members
GET {{base}}/groups/1/members
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 15. Group balances (simplified:true when group has simplify_debts enabled)
GET {{base}}/groups/1/balances
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 4: EXPENSES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### 16. Create expense — Equal split
POST {{base}}/expenses
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Dinner at Nobu",
  "amount": 120.00,
  "currency": "USD",
  "expense_date": "2026-06-11",
  "group_id": 1,
  "split_method": "equal",
  "payers": [
    { "user_id": 1, "amount_paid": 120.00 }
  ],
  "participants": [
    { "user_id": 1 },
    { "user_id": 2 }
  ]
}

###

### 17. Create expense — Percentage split
POST {{base}}/expenses
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Hotel Room",
  "amount": 300.00,
  "expense_date": "2026-06-11",
  "group_id": 1,
  "split_method": "percentage",
  "payers": [{ "user_id": 1, "amount_paid": 300.00 }],
  "participants": [
    { "user_id": 1, "percentage": 60 },
    { "user_id": 2, "percentage": 40 }
  ]
}

###

### 18. Create expense — Itemized
POST {{base}}/expenses
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Restaurant Receipt",
  "amount": 100.00,
  "expense_date": "2026-06-11",
  "group_id": 1,
  "split_method": "itemized",
  "payers": [{ "user_id": 1, "amount_paid": 100.00 }],
  "participants": [{ "user_id": 1 }, { "user_id": 2 }],
  "items": [
    { "name": "Steak",  "amount": 45.00, "assigned_to": [1] },
    { "name": "Pasta",  "amount": 30.00, "assigned_to": [2] },
    { "name": "Wine",   "amount": 25.00, "assigned_to": [1, 2] }
  ]
}

###

### 19. List expenses
GET {{base}}/expenses
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 5: BALANCES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### 20. My overall balances
GET {{base}}/balances
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 21. Balance breakdown per person
GET {{base}}/balances/breakdown
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 6: BILLS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### 22. Create bill
POST {{base}}/bills
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Electricity June",
  "amount": 90.00,
  "due_date": "2026-06-20",
  "group_id": 1,
  "reminder_days": [1, 3, 7]
}

###

### 23. List bills
GET {{base}}/bills
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 24. Mark bill paid (replace 1 with bill id)
POST {{base}}/bills/1/pay
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "payment_method": "bank_transfer"
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 7: SETTLEMENTS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### 25. Record settlement (settle up)
POST {{base}}/settlements
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "payee_id": 2,
  "group_id": 1,
  "amount": 60.00,
  "currency": "USD",
  "payment_method": "venmo",
  "notes": "Settling dinner",
  "settlement_date": "2026-06-11"
}

###

### 26. Send payment request to someone
POST {{base}}/settlements/requests
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "debtor_id": 2,
  "amount": 30.00,
  "message": "Please pay me back for hotel!"
}

###

### 27. List payment requests
GET {{base}}/settlements/requests
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 8-9: FEED & NOTIFICATIONS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### 28. Activity feed (auto-populated after creating expenses, bills, settlements, group events)
GET {{base}}/activity
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 28b. Group activity feed
GET {{base}}/groups/1/activity
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 29. Notifications (auto-created on events — respects notification settings & group mute)
GET {{base}}/notifications
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 30. Notification unread count
GET {{base}}/notifications/unread-count
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 10-11: REPORTS & DASHBOARD
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### 31. Personal report
GET {{base}}/reports/personal?from=2026-06-01&to=2026-06-30
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 32. Group report
GET {{base}}/reports/group/1?from=2026-06-01
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 33. Export CSV
GET {{base}}/reports/export?format=csv
Accept: */*
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 34. Dashboard (everything)
GET {{base}}/dashboard
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 35. List categories (system + your custom ones)
GET {{base}}/categories
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# MISSING #1: CUSTOM CATEGORIES CRUD
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### 36. Create custom category
POST {{base}}/categories
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pet Care",
  "icon": "paw-print",
  "color": "#a855f7"
}

###

### 37. Update custom category (replace 1 with your category id)
PUT {{base}}/categories/1
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pet Expenses",
  "color": "#7c3aed"
}

###

### 38. Delete custom category (replace 1 with your category id)
DELETE {{base}}/categories/1
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# MISSING #2: PAYMENT DEEP LINKS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### 39. Generate Venmo / PayPal / CashApp / Zelle deep links
### Replace payee_id with the user id of the person you're paying
GET {{base}}/settlements/deeplink?payee_id=2&amount=45.00&note=Settling%20dinner
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# MISSING #3: GROUP PHOTO UPLOAD
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### 40. Upload group cover photo (replace 1 with your group id)
### NOTE: Use Postman for file uploads — VS Code REST Client has limited multipart support
POST {{base}}/groups/1/photo
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----FormBoundary

------FormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="photo"; filename="cover.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./cover.jpg
------FormBoundary--

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# MISSING #4: PER-GROUP NOTIFICATION MUTE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### 41. Mute notifications for a group (replace 1 with your group id)
PUT {{base}}/groups/1/mute-notifications
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "muted": true
}

###

### 42. Unmute notifications for a group
PUT {{base}}/groups/1/mute-notifications
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "muted": false
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# MISSING #5: USER SEARCH
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### 43. Search users by name or email
GET {{base}}/users/search?q=john
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 44. Search users and exclude members already in a group
GET {{base}}/users/search?q=john&exclude_group_id=1
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# MISSING #6: ENHANCED PERSONAL REPORT
# (now includes by_group + balance_trend)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### 45. Personal report — full (with spend_by_group + balance_trend)
GET {{base}}/reports/personal?from=2026-06-01&to=2026-06-30
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 46. Personal report — last 3 months
GET {{base}}/reports/personal?from=2026-04-01&to=2026-06-30
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

